# The embedded UI is hashed, not just served. `capsHash` is computed over the
# bytes of pkg/aboard/web/views/*.spec.json, and `aboard capabilities --check`
# fails when the committed skill reference was generated for a different hash.
# A line-ending conversion (a Windows autocrlf checkout rewriting LF -> CRLF)
# changes those bytes, so the check would fail on the Windows CI runner for a
# tree that is byte-identical to the one that passed on Linux. Treat the whole
# embedded tree as text git must not touch.
pkg/aboard/web/** -text

# Same reason, plus these are fixtures compared byte-for-byte: the recipe
# precedence trees under testdata/, and the example board `aboard init
# --example` seeds from, which is embedded at pkg/aboard/example/ rather than
# living in testdata/ so that a `go install` binary carries it.
testdata/** -text
pkg/aboard/example/** -text

# The generated files are written by the binary and diffed against the working
# tree by `make caps`. A rewritten line ending would show as a diff on every
# checkout on the other platform.
.claude/skills/aboard/references/*.generated.md -text
